# How git must treat these files, stated rather than guessed.
#
# Without this, git falls back to its own heuristic for what is binary, and that
# heuristic runs against `core.autocrlf`. On a Windows machine with autocrlf on, a file
# git decides is text has every LF rewritten to CRLF on checkout — which for a PNG
# changes the bytes while barely changing the size, so the result is a file of roughly
# the right length that no longer decodes as an image. It looks like a broken upload and
# is nothing of the kind.
#
# So the rule is declared here, where it travels with the repository and applies on
# every machine, rather than depending on each developer's global git configuration.

# Text files: stored with LF, checked out however the platform wants.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary. Never touched, never diffed as text, never line-ending converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.eot binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
